    <string name="about_dialog_body">A calm, premium weather app built with Kotlin and Jetpack Compose.\n\nAccurate forecasts, a thoughtful design system and no clutter. Weather for a better tomorrow.</string>
    <string name="privacy_dialog_body">SKYORA has no accounts, no analytics and no advertising. Your saved cities, preferences and last forecast are stored only on this device.\n\nWhen you use location, your coordinates are sent to Open-Meteo to request a forecast. Search terms go to Open-Meteo’s geocoding service. Location access is optional and can be revoked at any time in Android settings.</string>
    <string name="attribution_dialog_body">Weather data by Open-Meteo (open-meteo.com), provided under the CC BY 4.0 licence. City search data is provided by Open-Meteo under CC BY-NC 4.0.\n\nThe free Open-Meteo API is intended for non-commercial use and has fair-use limits (currently around 10,000 calls per day). Review Open-Meteo’s terms and obtain an appropriate plan before any commercial release.\n\nSKYORA converts temperatures and wind speeds to your selected units, rounds values for display, and maps WMO weather codes to readable descriptions. No data is changed beyond those display transformations.</string>
    <string name="attribution_dialog_title">Weather data &amp; licences</string>
    <string name="privacy_dialog_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_dialog_title">About SKYORA</string>
