    <string name="reliability_section_help">If updates feel late</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_body">SKYORA uses standard Android background work, so it needs no setup. Some manufacturers add extra limits on top; if that applies to this device, these steps usually help.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_xiaomi">Xiaomi / Redmi / POCO: Settings › Apps › Manage apps › SKYORA › Battery saver → No restrictions, and enable Autostart.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_huawei">Huawei / Honor: Settings › Battery › App launch › SKYORA → Manage manually, then allow Auto-launch and running in the background.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_oppo">Oppo / Realme / OnePlus: Settings › Battery › App battery management › SKYORA → allow background activity and auto-launch.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_vivo">Vivo / iQOO: Settings › Battery › Background power consumption management › SKYORA → allow high background power usage.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_samsung">Samsung: Settings › Battery › Background usage limits → add SKYORA to Never sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="reliability_help_generic">Open the app info screen and check that battery usage is unrestricted and background data is allowed.</string>
